00:12:23.235 --> 00:12:27.795
So I hope that's helpful and I look
forward to questions, but I just wanna

00:12:27.795 --> 00:12:32.204
stress again that reading is a phenomenal
way to increase your vocabulary.

00:12:32.475 --> 00:12:38.355
If you aren't yet at a stage where you
can read a book, a paper book, then using

00:12:38.355 --> 00:12:40.865
something like LingQ can be quite helpful.

00:12:41.324 --> 00:12:49.185
So to summarize, reading is a, is perhaps
the best way to acquire more vocabulary.

00:12:49.365 --> 00:12:50.265
It's very efficient.

00:12:50.415 --> 00:12:51.405
You're looking things up.

00:12:51.435 --> 00:12:55.064
Even if you forget it, you'll see
it again and eventually it becomes

00:12:55.064 --> 00:12:56.415
part of your passive vocabulary.

00:12:56.834 --> 00:13:03.285
So, but reading can be done extensively or
intensively, and I think it's best to vary

00:13:03.765 --> 00:13:05.865
extensive reading with intensive reading.

00:13:05.865 --> 00:13:09.915
Maybe you spend more time on extensive
reading, but you should probably be

00:13:09.935 --> 00:13:12.030
guided by what you feel like doing.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:15.930
'causeCif you enjoy the activity
that you're involved in, you're

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:17.280
more likely to stay with it.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:20.370
You're more likely to learn if
you're enjoying the activity.

